                        "content": "Oral bethanechol chloride is prescribed for the client. The nurse would instruct the client to take this medication at which time?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nAdministration of bethanechol chloride with food can cause nausea and vomiting. To avoid this problem, oral doses need to be administered 1 hour before meals or 2 hours after meals. Therefore, all other options are incorrect.",
