                        "content": "A client who has had a prostatectomy is complaining of pain from bladder spasms. The nurse checks the primary health care provider's prescription sheet and expects to see which medication prescribed to treat the problem?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nBladder spasms after prostatectomy are treated with antispasmodic medications, such as oxybutynin. Opioid analgesics such as morphine sulfate, hydromorphone, and meperidine hydrochloride usually are not effective in treating pain caused by spasms.",
                        "id": "1a5858f9836b471c9a36e72ecfe6509f",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
