                        "content": "Parenteral bethanechol chloride is prescribed for a client with urinary retention. The nurse would plan to administer this medication by which route?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe injectable form of bethanechol chloride is intended for subcutaneous administration only. Bethanechol must never be injected intramuscularly or intravenously because the resulting high medication level can cause severe toxicity, resulting in bloody diarrhea, bradycardia, profound hypotension, and cardiovascular collapse.",
                        "id": "1d8003fdc7fd446b99c6bb6e5d0abbcb",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
